 75   c  ABST$The experimental nuclear spectroscopic data for known nuclides of 
 75  2c  mass number 75 (Fe, Co, Ni, Cu, Zn, Ga, Ge, As, Se, Br, Kr, Rb, Sr)    
 75  3c  have been evaluated and presented together with Adopted properties for 
 75  4c  levels and { |g rays}. New high-spin data are available for {+75}Ga,   
 75  5c  and {+75}Rb; and lifetime data for high-spin states in {+75}Br and     
 75  6c  {+75}Kr. For |DJ=1, M1+E2 transitions in two rotational bands in       
 75  7c  {+75}Kr, several B(E2)(W.u.) values are anomalously high, deviating by 
 75  8c  2-3 |s values from currently accepted RUL(E2)=300. In the opinion of   
 75  9c  the evaluators, there is need to remeasure level lifetimes and         
 75  Ac  multipole mixing ratios in {+75}Kr to resolve this serious             
 75  Bc  discrepancy.  New precise single-particle transfer cross section data  
 75  Cc  are available for {+75}Ga, {+75}Ge, {+75}As and {+75}Se from several   
 75  Dc  different reactions (2009Ka06,2008Sc03); these data give information   
 75  Ec  for occupancy of valence neutron orbitals in the ground states of      
 75  Fc  target nuclides: {+76}Ge, {+76}Se and {+78}Se. No significant new data 
 75  Gc  since the 1999 Nuclear Data Sheets for A=75 have been reported for     
 75  Hc  {+75}As and {+75}Se. No data are yet available for excited states in   
 75  Ic  {+75}Co, {+75}Ni and {+75}Sr. For {+75}Fe, only the isotopic           
 75  Jc  identification is made with one observed event The radioactive decay   
 75  Kc  schemes of {+75}Co and {+75}Ni are unknown while those for {+75}Rb and 
 75  Lc  {+75}Sr are incomplete. This work supersedes the data presented in the 
 75  Mc  previous Nuclear Data Sheets evaluation of A=75 published by 1999Fa05. 
 75   c  CUT$Literature available up to June 30, 2013, has been consulted. The  
 75  2c  bibliographic source is mainly the NSR database at Brookhaven National 
 75  3c  Laboratory webpage: www.nndc.bnl.gov/nsr/                              
